fix(core): resolve initPromise after world/room creation completes

The initPromise was being resolved prematurely after adapter initialization
but before world and room entities were created. This caused plugins waiting
on initPromise to access database operations that could fail due to missing
foreign key references.

Changes:
- Move initResolver() call to after all initialization steps complete
- Ensure world entity creation (lines 504-515) happens before promise resolves
- Ensure room entity creation (lines 517-537) happens before promise resolves
- Add comprehensive documentation about proper plugin initialization patterns

Plugins should NOT await initPromise in their init() function (causes deadlock).
Instead, spawn background tasks that wait on initPromise:

  // ✅ CORRECT
  init: async (_, runtime) => {
    runtime.initPromise.then(async () => {
      // Safe to access world/room entities
    });
  }

  // ❌ WRONG - causes deadlock
  init: async (_, runtime) => {
    await runtime.initPromise;
  }

