- All 8 initPromise-specific tests pass
- No regressions introduced

feat(rust): improved WASM foundation with structured errors and JS shims

This PR introduces several improvements to the Rust WASM bindings:

## Structured Error Handling (WasmError)

Instead of returning opaque JS error strings, WASM bindings now return
structured WasmError objects with:
- `code`: Programmatic error code (PARSE_ERROR, VALIDATION_ERROR, etc.)
- `message`: Human-readable error description
- `source`: Optional source context (field name, parameter, etc.)

JavaScript can now handle errors programmatically:
```javascript
try {
    const runtime = WasmAgentRuntime.create('invalid json');
} catch (e) {
    if (e.code === 'PARSE_ERROR') {
        console.log(`Parse error in ${e.source}: ${e.message}`);
    }
}
```

## JS Model Handler Shim (JsModelHandler)

A new pattern for wrapping JavaScript callbacks as type-safe Rust interfaces:

```javascript
const handler = new JsModelHandler({
    handle: async (paramsJson) => {
        const params = JSON.parse(paramsJson);
        // Call your LLM API
        return JSON.stringify({ text: response });
    }
});
runtime.registerModelHandler('TEXT_LARGE', handler);
```

This enables:
- Type-safe callback registration
- Proper async/Promise handling
- Clean error propagation from JS to Rust

## Module Reorganization

Restructured wasm module into:
- `wasm/mod.rs`: Main bindings (WasmAgentRuntime, type wrappers, utilities)
- `wasm/error.rs`: WasmError and WasmResultExt trait
- `wasm/shims/`: JS callback wrappers (JsModelHandler)

## WASM Test Infrastructure

Added comprehensive wasm_bindgen_test based tests covering:
- Error creation and formatting
- JsModelHandler creation and validation
- Type wrapper serialization round-trips
- Runtime lifecycle

## Cargo.toml Improvements

Platform-specific dev dependencies for cleaner separation:
- tokio for native tests
- wasm-bindgen-test for WASM tests

fix(scripts): remove rename-collapsed self-recursion in asset-cdn alias + correct REPO_ROOT path in write-homepage-release-data

asset-cdn.mjs:
  The 2f1b81f887 rename collapsed
    export function resolveMiladyAssetBaseUrls(options = {}) {
      return resolveElizaAssetBaseUrls(options);
    }
  into a self-referential
    export function resolveElizaAssetBaseUrls(options = {}) {
      return resolveElizaAssetBaseUrls(options);
    }
  which (a) is a parse-error-causing duplicate export of the same name
  already defined above, and (b) would infinite-loop if any caller
  imported it. The alias is no longer needed since the canonical
  function is already exported. Drop the alias entirely.

write-homepage-release-data.mjs:
  REPO_ROOT was set to `path.resolve(SCRIPT_DIR, "..")` — that resolves
  to packages/app-core/scripts (the parent of `lib/`), not the repo
  root. The script was reading/writing files relative to the wrong
  base. Fix to `path.resolve(SCRIPT_DIR, "..", "..", "..")` (repo root).

